# Review Protocol

Prioritize correctness, security, data loss, privacy, authentication, authorization,
race conditions, broken tests, missing migrations, dependency risk, and behavior
regressions.

Avoid style-only review unless style hides a real defect. Cite exact files, symbols,
line numbers, commands, and reproduction steps where possible.

If no actionable issue is found, say "no high-confidence issues found" and list any
remaining test gaps or residual risks.
